The copy constructor already does the least work it can: it copies the `FieldBase` sub-object and four plain members. I don't know `FieldBase`'s layout, so I can't safely restructure that copy. The only change here is formatting, and it does not change the compiled code.

Real speedups would have to come from elsewhere:
- avoiding `Field` copies at the call sites (moves or references);
- giving `FieldBase` a cheaper copy.

```cpp
Field::Field(const Field &field)
    : FieldBase(field),
      profile(field.profile),
      profileIndex(field.profileIndex),
      type(field.type),
      isFieldExpanded(field.isFieldExpanded)
{}
```